<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lars Porsenna</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">late 6th century BCE</span> · Also known as Porsena</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lars Porsenna was an Etruscan king of Clusium (modern Chiusi) who, in Roman tradition, attacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> around 508 BCE after the expulsion of its last king, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarquinius-superbus">Tarquinius Superbus</a>. Roman legends of Horatius at the bridge, Mucius Scaevola and Cloelia are set during his siege. Some ancient writers suggest he actually captured the city, and the stories may preserve a real period of Etruscan control.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lars-porsenna.jpg" alt="Lars Porsenna" width="320" height="327" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Published by Guillaume Rouille (1518?-1589) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lars_Porsena.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
